-- Castle Nathria (map 2296) -- gameobject SPAWN rows, transcoded from the Shadowlands-era
-- source dump (SLDB_902_world_2021_03_12.sql) filtered to map=2296, with a same-guid
-- `state` correction applied from 2021_03_15_00_world_shriekwing.sql (later-dated, supersedes
-- the main dump's state for that one door). 2021_03_18_00_world_darkvein.sql,
-- 2021_03_15_01_world_sl_dung.sql (map 2285, not this raid) and the large
-- 2021_03_18_02_world_cre_gob_data.sql supplement were checked and contain no relevant
-- gameobject SPAWN rows (template/script-level data only) -- not applied here.
--
-- GUID remap: source guids are a scattered/unrelated id space and are NOT reused. Fresh
-- guids are assigned sequentially (15100003+) ordered by source guid.
--
-- spawnMask=1 / phaseMask=1 for all rows (single baseline difficulty). rotation0-3 are
-- copied straight through -- the source dump already uses the same quaternion
-- representation as 3.3.5. ScriptName='' / VerifiedBuild=NULL for all rows (template-level
-- concern, handled elsewhere). Comment = GO name where resolvable from the source dump's
-- own `gameobject_template` rows for the known Nathria entry ids, else ''. NOTE: this
-- source dump's gameobject_template.name is Russian-localized for player-facing objects
-- (some further mangled by a charset mishap already present in the source bytes); non-ASCII
-- names were dropped to '' rather than emit unreadable/garbled Comment text. Technical
-- art-asset names (collision volumes, doodad helpers) were never localized and come through
-- clean.
--
-- 780 rows. Apply to acore_world.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- gameobject
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- DEDUPE (2026-07-19, post first in-game test): the source dump contained systematically
-- duplicated GO spawn rows (~6 copies of most objects; 487 of the original 780 rows were
-- same-entry duplicates within 3 yd). Deduplicated keep-first; guids reassigned sequentially.
-- The DELETE below intentionally still covers the ORIGINAL full guid range 15100003-15100782
-- so re-running this file also purges the duplicate rows from an earlier import.


DELETE FROM `gameobject` WHERE `guid` BETWEEN 15100003 AND 15100782;

